-- A host's thing held by a `with`, the same for every effect: an open
-- file, a socket, a process, a canvas -- what must be let go of.  Each
-- has its own `with`: `withFile`, `withProcess`, `Net.withConnection`,
-- and so on.  In a `do` block a `with` is a statement, `with withFile
-- path o as f do`, the statements under it its body.  Each one:
--
-- 1. acquires the thing;
-- 2. runs the body with it, a `With s r` in a region `s` of its own;
-- 3. releases it when the body ends;
-- 4. comes to what the body came to.
--
-- ```haskell
-- import co
-- import exception
-- import std.filesystem
-- import std.path
--
-- firstLine : {e : HFunctor}
--           -> {{disk : filesystem <: e}}
--           -> {{fx : exception FileError <: e}}
--           -> String
--           -> Co e (Either FileError (Maybe String))
-- firstLine path = withFile path { access = Read } (\f -> readLine f)
-- ```
--
-- The body is polymorphic in `s`, and what it comes to is of a type bound
-- outside it, so a `With s r` cannot leave the body, as Haskell's `ST`
-- keeps its references in: `withFile path o (\f -> pure f)` is a type
-- error (E0311).  There is one `With` for every effect, so a `with` of one
-- effect may hand its thing to an operation of another by value -- a
-- `<canvas>` found by browser.dom, drawn on by browser.gpu -- and neither
-- keeps it.
--
-- A `with` comes to what its body came to, and nothing else: a thing not
-- acquired is no answer of the body's, so it is thrown, over the
-- `exception` effect, the body not run -- a `with` asks for `exception
-- err` besides its own effect, and `try` can catch it.  A thing not
-- released is thrown once the body has ended, what it came to abandoned.
-- `held` is the `with` of a thing that is always had and let go of -- a
-- standard stream, the page's document -- which throws nothing.
--
-- The thing is the host's own, a foreign value with a finalizer, so a
-- body left otherwise -- a throw heard outside it, a handler between that
-- drops the continuation -- lets go of it where the program drops its
-- last reference to it; `scoped` adds nothing for that.
--
-- `With` is exposed without its tag: no program makes one, and `scoped
-- acquire release body` and `held acquire release body` are the only ways
-- to make one.  A library wraps one around its own operations acquiring
-- and releasing the thing, as std.filesystem does:
--
-- ```haskell
-- withFile : {e : HFunctor} -> {a : Type} -> {{ev : filesystem <: e}}
--          -> {{ex : exception FileError <: e}}
--          -> String -> OpenOptions
--          -> ({s : Type} -> With s OpenFile -> Co e a)
--          -> Co e a
-- withFile path o body = scoped (opened path o) closed body
--
-- readLine : {e : HFunctor} -> {s : Type} -> {{ev : filesystem <: e}}
--          -> With s OpenFile -> Co e (Either FileError (Maybe String))
-- readLine f = op (ev (ReadLine (inside f) (\r -> r))) val
-- ```
--
-- - It exposes that `withX` alone, never the bare acquire, as a bare host
--   value given `scoped` is a use after its close.
-- - Its operations take the `With s a`, and give the thing to a provider
--   operation by `inside`, which takes it out for that operation and
--   nothing else.
-- - What lives as long as the program, such as a GPU device, is held by a
--   `with` at the top of `main`.
--
-- How a provider lets the thing go is a provider's scoped operations'.

module resource (With, scoped, held, inside)

import co
import exception

-- | A host's thing, held in the region `s` by a `with` (`scoped`,
-- | `held`).
data With (s : Type) a = MkWith a

-- | The thing a `with` holds, for a provider operation given it: a
-- | library's operation on a `With s a` takes it out here and gives it
-- | to the operation, and nothing else does.
inside : {s : Type} -> {a : Type} -> With s a -> a
inside (MkWith x) = x

-- (what the body came to, once the thing is released; a release that
-- failed, thrown)
releasedTo : {e : HFunctor}
           -> {err a : Type}
           -> {{ex : exception err <: e}}
           -> a
           -> Either err Unit
           -> Co e a
releasedTo v (Right u) = pure v
releasedTo v (Left err) = throw err

-- (the body run with the thing, then the thing released; a thing not
-- acquired, thrown)
heldBy : {e : HFunctor}
       -> {err r a : Type}
       -> {{ex : exception err <: e}}
       -> (r -> Co e (Either err Unit))
       -> ({s : Type} -> With s r -> Co e a)
       -> Either err r
       -> Co e a
heldBy release body (Left err) = throw err
heldBy release body (Right x) =
  bind
    (body (s := r) (MkWith x))
    (\v -> bind (release x) (releasedTo v))

-- | The thing `acquire` gives, held by `body` in a region of its own --
-- | it is not kept past it -- and released by `release` when `body`
-- | ends: what it came to.  A thing not acquired is thrown, the body
-- | not run; one not released is thrown once the body has ended, what
-- | it came to abandoned.  Should `body` be left otherwise -- a throw
-- | heard outside it, a handler between that drops the continuation --
-- | the thing is let go of where the program drops its last reference
-- | to it, as its provider says.
scoped : {e : HFunctor}
       -> {err r a : Type}
       -> {{ex : exception err <: e}}
       -> Co e (Either err r)
       -> (r -> Co e (Either err Unit))
       -> ({s : Type} -> With s r -> Co e a)
       -> Co e a
scoped acquire release body = bind acquire (heldBy release body)

-- (the body run with the thing, then the thing let go of)
letGoAfter : {e : HFunctor}
           -> {r a : Type}
           -> (r -> Co e Unit)
           -> ({s : Type} -> With s r -> Co e a)
           -> r
           -> Co e a
letGoAfter release body x =
  bind (body (s := r) (MkWith x)) (\v -> bind (release x) (\u -> pure v))

-- | The thing `acquire` gives, which it always does, held by `body` in
-- | a region of its own and let go of by `release` when `body` ends,
-- | which always goes: what the body came to.  The `with` of a thing
-- | the program is never without: a standard stream, the page's
-- | document.
held : {e : HFunctor}
     -> {r a : Type}
     -> Co e r
     -> (r -> Co e Unit)
     -> ({s : Type} -> With s r -> Co e a)
     -> Co e a
held acquire release body = bind acquire (letGoAfter release body)
